1
00:05:17,777 --> 00:05:23,777
The beloved masterpiece comes to life.

2
00:10:35,555 --> 00:10:41,555
The Chronicles of Narnia: The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe is a
adventure, family, fantasy film directed by Andrew Adamson.

3
00:15:53,333 --> 00:15:59,333
Siblings Lucy, Edmund, Susan and Peter step through a
magical wardrobe and find the land of Narnia.

4
00:21:11,111 --> 00:21:17,111
There, they discover a charming, once peaceful kingdom that has been
plunged into eternal winter by the evil White Witch, Jadis.

5
00:26:28,888 --> 00:26:34,888
Aided by the wise and magnificent lion, Aslan, the children lead Narnia into a
spectacular, climactic battle to be free of the Witch's glacial powers forever.

6
00:31:46,666 --> 00:31:52,666
Peter Pevensie, played by William Moseley.

7
00:37:04,444 --> 00:37:10,444
Susan Pevensie, played by Anna Popplewell.

8
00:42:22,222 --> 00:42:28,222
Edmund Pevensie, played by Skandar Keynes.

9
00:47:40,000 --> 00:47:46,000
Lucy Pevensie, played by Georgie Henley.

10
00:52:57,777 --> 00:53:03,777
Aslan (voice), played by Liam Neeson.

11
00:58:15,555 --> 00:58:21,555
White Witch, played by Tilda Swinton.

12
01:03:33,333 --> 01:03:39,333
The Chronicles of Narnia: The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe is a 2005 high fantasy film directed by Andrew Adamson, who co-wrote the screenplay with Ann Peacock and the writing team of Christopher Markus
and Stephen McFeely, based on the 1950 novel The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe, the first published and second chronological novel in the children's book series The Chronicles of Narnia by C.

13
01:08:51,111 --> 01:08:57,111
The film is the first installment in The Chronicles of Narnia film series.

14
01:14:08,888 --> 01:14:14,888
It was produced by Walt Disney Pictures and Walden Media, and
distributed by Buena Vista Pictures Distribution.

15
01:19:26,666 --> 01:19:32,666
William Moseley, Anna Popplewell, Skandar Keynes, and Georgie Henley play Peter, Susan, Edmund, and Lucy Pevensie, four British children evacuated during the Blitz to the countryside, who find
a wardrobe that leads to the fantasy world of Narnia, where they ally with the lion Aslan (voiced by Liam Neeson) against the forces of Jadis, the White Witch (Tilda Swinton).

16
01:24:44,444 --> 01:24:50,444
The Chronicles of Narnia: The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe premiered on 7 December 2005, selected for the Royal Film
Performance, before it was theatrically released on 8 December in the United Kingdom and 9 December in the United States.

17
01:30:02,222 --> 01:30:08,222
The film was a critical and commercial success, grossing $745 million worldwide against a
$180 million budget and becoming the third-highest-grossing film of 2005.

18
01:35:20,000 --> 01:35:26,000
An extended edition was released on 12 December 2006, on DVD.

19
01:40:37,777 --> 01:40:43,777
Combining both releases of the film, in regular and extended edition, it was the third-best-selling and
first-highest-grossing DVD in North America in 2006, taking in $332.7 million that year.

20
01:45:55,555 --> 01:46:01,555
At the 78th Academy Awards, the film won for Best Makeup and was nominated for Best Sound Mixing and Best Visual Effects, while at the 59th
BAFTA Awards, it won for Best Makeup and Hair and was nominated for Best Costume Design and Best Special Visual Effects.

21
01:51:13,333 --> 01:51:19,333
The score was nominated for Best Original Score and the song "Wunderkind" by Alanis
Morissette was nominated for Best Original Song at the 63rd Golden Globe Awards.

22
01:56:31,111 --> 01:56:37,111
The score was also nominated for Best Score Soundtrack Album for Motion Picture, Television or Other Visual Media and the song "Can't Take It In"
by Imogen Heap was nominated for Best Song Written For Motion Picture, Television or Other Visual Media at the 49th Grammy Awards.

23
02:01:48,888 --> 02:01:54,888
The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe was followed by Prince Caspian in 2008 and The Voyage
of the Dawn Treader in 2010 to diminishing critical and financial reception.

24
02:07:06,666 --> 02:07:12,666
Nevertheless, the three films grossed a total of $1.5 billion worldwide.

25
02:12:24,444 --> 02:12:30,444
The film explores themes of witch, sibling relationship, saving
the world, based on novel or book, self sacrifice.

26
02:17:42,222 --> 02:17:48,222
The tone is mind_bending.
